    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e95cc25b",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "racially_charged_statement",
      "label": "Racially Charged Statement",
      "description": "The text overlay accuses South Africans of being complicit in or tolerant of theft by outsiders, using a dehumanizing and economically reductive stereotype. This statement relies on the implicit knowledge that South Africans are a distinct racial and national group, and that the meme's author is making a racially charged accusation against them. The statement also implies a false assumption about the attitudes of the majority of South Africans toward economic injustice and theft.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_93cf1a12",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "cyril",
      "label": "Cyril Ramaphosa",
      "description": "Cyril Ramaphosa is the President of South Africa. The text 'see... i told you cyril' implies that the speaker is addressing or referencing him, likely in the context of a political or economic controversy. The meme uses his name to target him as a representative of the South African government or people, which is a form of political satire or accusation. This requires background knowledge of who Cyril Ramaphosa is and his role in South African politics.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7db5be3a",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "south_africa",
      "label": "South Africa",
      "description": "The meme references South Africa as the location and target of the accusation. The statement 'the majority in sa do not mind us stealing from them' requires background knowledge of South Africa as a country with a complex history of colonialism, apartheid, and economic inequality. The meme uses this knowledge to frame the accusation as a racially charged economic grievance, implying that South Africans are passive recipients of exploitation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c4da949e",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "economic_exploitation_stereotype",
      "label": "Economic Exploitation Stereotype",
      "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Black South Africans are passive recipients of economic exploitation and theft by outsiders. This stereotype is a form of racialized economic grievance that frames Black South Africans as economically dependent and complicit in or tolerant of theft. This requires background knowledge of the historical and contemporary economic dynamics in South Africa, including the legacy of apartheid and the current economic challenges faced by the country.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_93e29b0d",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "racial_hierarchy_stereotype",
      "label": "Racial Hierarchy Stereotype",
      "description": "The meme reinforces a harmful narrative of racial hierarchy and economic victimhood by portraying Black South Africans as passive recipients of exploitation. This stereotype is based on the implicit knowledge that racial hierarchies exist and that Black people are often portrayed as inferior or less capable in economic contexts. The meme uses this knowledge to justify the accusation and to frame the speaker's attitude as one of contempt and superiority.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_67a4fb05",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "hateful_meme",
      "label": "Hateful Meme",
      "description": "The meme is classified as hateful because it attacks a specific racial group based on protected characteristics. This requires background knowledge of the concept of hate speech and the impact of racially charged language on marginalized communities. The meme's intent is to provoke division and hostility by weaponizing racialized economic grievances, which is a form of hate speech.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0336d72c",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "contempt",
      "label": "expression of contempt",
      "description": "The man in the foreground is laughing broadly with an open mouth and a triumphant expression, which, in context of the racially charged text, conveys a sense of superiority and disdain toward the group being accused. His facial expression is not one of genuine amusement but rather one of contemptuous triumph, suggesting he views the situation as a victory or confirmation of his belief.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e20d1a40",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_001",
      "label": "The speaker is mapped onto the man in the foreground",
      "description": "The text 'see... i told you cyril.' implies that the man in the foreground is the speaker or is being referenced as the person who made the statement. The visual of the man laughing broadly is juxtaposed with the text to project the identity of the speaker onto him, making him the embodiment of the hateful statement. This is an analogical mapping where the textual entity 'cyril' (implied speaker) is mapped onto the visual entity 'man_in_foreground'.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a589f89a",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the scene as the speaker of the racially charged statement",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the man in the foreground is depicted as the speaker of the hateful statement. The text 'see... i told you cyril.' implies that the user is identifying with or imagining themselves as the person making the accusation, projecting their own viewpoint or attitude onto the visual and textual elements of the meme. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictics like 'you' or 'me' in the text, but the framing of the meme as a direct address ('see... i told you') creates an implicit projection of the user as the one who is 'telling' or 'showing' the statement to Cyril Ramaphosa, thereby positioning the user as the speaker or the one who holds the viewpoint being expressed. This projection is onto the scene, which includes both the visual material (the laughing man) and the textual material (the hateful statement), making the scene the primary entity onto which the user is projected.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_234791e4",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme directly attacks a specific racial group (Black South Africans) based on protected characteristics, using racially charged language and imagery to dehumanize and stereotype them. The text accuses them of being complicit in or tolerant of theft by outsiders, reinforcing harmful narratives of racial hierarchy and economic victimhood. The visual of the laughing man juxtaposed with the text amplifies the message of contempt and superiority, making it a hateful meme that attacks a specific racial group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2f0c864b",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The intended audience is individuals who hold or are exposed to racially charged, economically reductive, and politically divisive narratives about South Africans, particularly those who support or sympathize with the stereotype that Black South Africans are passive recipients of exploitation and tolerant of theft by outsiders. The meme targets those who may identify with or propagate the 'racial hierarchy' and 'economic exploitation stereotype' tropes, and who are likely to engage with or share content that weaponizes racialized economic grievances. The reference to 'Cyril' (Cyril Ramaphosa) indicates the audience may include politically aware South Africans or international observers familiar with South African politics, who are being targeted with a hateful message that frames the South African government or people as complicit in or tolerant of economic injustice. The visual of the laughing man is used to project contempt and superiority, appealing to an audience that finds satisfaction in dehumanizing and stereotyping Black South Africans.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f7cee154"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    }
  ]
